{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"verdict\": \"both_partly\",\n  \"quotes\": [\n    \"We first examined the relationship between LFP spectral power and GI RPC scores in trials without FOG, in the DOPAOFF condition, in both patients with PD groups (Supplementary Fig S3).\",\n    \"The analysis included data from 267 dipoles located within the STN (139 and 128 in the posterior and central STN, respectively), comprising 946 traces (725 in FOG-NOBS and 221 in FOG-OBS patients; see Figs 1D and 4).\",\n    \"In the 12 FOG-OBS patients with PD, we recorded 99 trials where a FOG event occurred in the DOPAOFF condition (FOG-OBS+ trials), with a median onset of 8 steps (interquartile range [IQR] = 6–11.5) after GI, and a total of 263 FOG episodes (Fig 1E–G).\",\n    \"To explore STN dysfunction linked to FOG, we compared trials with freezing (FOG-OBS+ trials) to those without (FOG-OBS− trials) in FOG-OBS patients with PD (DOPAOFF condition; Fig 6).\",\n    \"These changes were evident as early as the GI phase, prior to the observable FOG onset.\",\n    \"FOG-OBS patients with PD show early, identifiable changes in GI and STN activity patterns up to 19 seconds before FOG.\",\n    \"STN-LFPs data were first high-pass filtered at 1 Hz, notch filtered at 50 Hz, and epoched from 2 seconds before the cue to the end of the second swing phase.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"双方各有部分依据。报告的说法有依据：论文首先分析了没有FOG发生的步态试次中的STN-LFP与步态启动参数之间的关系，明确将这部分结果用于研究FOG predisposition（易感性），因此将其视为FOG易感性证据是合理的。此外，LFP分析的时间窗口截至第二次摆动结束，并非实际冻结发生期间的直接神经记录。但指控者也有充分依据：论文并非只分析无冻结试次。研究明确纳入了99个随后发生FOG的步行试次，共检测到263次冻结事件，首次冻结中位发生于步态启动后8步。作者进一步专门比较了FOG阳性试次与阴性试次的STN-LFP关联，发现步态启动期的神经活动变化先于实际冻结发生，并将其解释为imminent FOG（即即将发生的冻结）的预测性特征。因此，这部分结果确实属于Pre-FOG事件关联证据，而不只是一般FOG易感性证据。综合而言，报告正确指出研究没有记录实际冻结期间的直接神经活动，但如果将整项研究主要归结为一般FOG易感性，而没有区分其对随后发生冻结的试次所进行的Pre-FOG分析，则是不完整的。故判定为both_partly。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "5dfa471f-b360-4f8d-9d1e-16c87a37240b", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261113T104608672768Z", "elapsed_seconds": 56.438, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T10:47:05.117578+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "983f448a1325b393abe1eb95f41ab82fe2e1602246186aee0d0b042b7843fea4", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "yi/local-codex-auth", "account_sha256": "b3efb6361563c139233ed7b7ef61a7c9afe0bd48d4eb3525dbe31956b024d6da", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261113T104608672768Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "a5321f691e94807dbd2f836d3ff19dc5e456ace4e11f295d6b4de83a8721be91"}}}
